# Real-user job: someone who already has MCP servers configured in their
# real ~/.claude.json opens kiln in a fresh project, browses what's
# available via /mcp, switches to the "ops" posture, and asks a strictly
# read-only question against one of their real servers (Grafana). Uses the
# real HOME (no @home scratch) on purpose, since the point is to exercise
# whatever the user already has configured; it writes nothing to user
# scope, only reads and asks read-only questions.
@real
@size 140x45
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SHOT ready
TYPE /mcp
KEY enter
SHOT mcp-dialog
KEY down
SHOT mcp-dialog-nav
KEY enter
SHOT mcp-dialog-detail
KEY esc
KEY esc
SHOT mcp-dialog-closed
TYPE /posture ops
KEY enter
SHOT posture-ops
TURN Using the Grafana MCP, list the configured datasources and say whether each is healthy. Read-only: do not create, update or delete anything.
SHOT investigated
TYPE /posture coding
KEY enter
SHOT posture-coding
